Package: shallows
Title: Well-Balanced Shallow Water Simulation on Raster Grids
Version: 0.1.0.9002
Authors@R: person("Michael", "Sumner", email = "mdsumner@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Prototype two-dimensional shallow water (Saint-Venant) solver on
    regular grids. First- or second-order finite volume scheme with the HLL
    Riemann solver and hydrostatic reconstruction (Audusse et al. 2004), so
    that lakes at rest are preserved exactly and depth stays non-negative over
    wetting and drying terrain. Manning bed friction, rain, wall and open
    boundaries, and a mass budget that closes to round-off. Includes analytic
    benchmark solutions (Ritter and Stoker dam breaks, Thacker paraboloid)
    used for validation.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/hypertidy/shallows, https://hypertidy.github.io/shallows/
